"""Keeps track of which functions of Blitz3D and BlitzPlus the test suite has to cover.

  suite_functions.py list [file]  Writes the list of functions to the file, or prints it without one.
  suite_functions.py pending      Writes a placeholder test for every function that is not implemented yet.
  suite_functions.py check        Fails if a function has no test, or a placeholder test is for something that exists now.

The list is not kept in the repository: it is made each time from the original sources in /third_party (the submodules
blitz3d and blitzplus_msvc2017), builtins.inc and the tables below, by read_list() for the tools that use it (the wiki,
the VS Code grammar) and by 'list' for the ones that need a file. A function the list gets wrong is fixed in the tables.

The list has one function per line: name, module, state (done or pending) and the signature, written like the
declaration of a function in BlitzLLVM:  Name:Result(parameter:Type, Out parameter:Type = default). A command without a
result has no ':Result', Out marks a parameter the command writes to and InOut one it reads and writes. The signatures
of the originals are converted from the type characters they are registered with (% # $). A function is done once it is in code_compiler/source/builtins.inc, or the compiler handles it.
Done functions have to be named by at least one test in tests/suite. Pending functions have a file of their own in
tests/suite/pending, which is expected to fail to compile until the function exists.
"""
